<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.11.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01934</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.11.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>77f9d50d-b8ec-49f1-9ee9-c7c0ea238c30</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_92d59337-3613-48cb-ba17-d11f71cb511e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00002"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> true statements about the graph that represents \(y=2x(x-11)\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00003">Correct! Its \(x\)-intercepts are at (0,0) and (11,0).The \(x\)-coordinate of its vertex is 5.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">The correct answers are: Its \(x\)-intercepts are at (0,0) and (11,0). The \(x\)-coordinate of its vertex is 5.5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e72a5230-87d9-4225-b0fc-194d6408af7d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00006"><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> equations whose graphs have a vertex with \(x\)-coordinate 2.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! \(y=(x-1)(x-3)\) and \( y=x(x-4)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00008">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00009">The correct answers are: Its \(x\)-intercepts are \(y=(x-1)(x-3)\), \(y=x(x-4)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1e77c74e-9e17-4703-b6f8-9cb42b073a3c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Three different equations are given. Refer to these equations to complete questions a–f.</para>
            <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable" id="table-00001">
              <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>Equation</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(x\)-intercept</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>\(x\)-coordinate of the vertex</emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00011">\(y=x(x-2)\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00012">a. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00013">b. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00014">\(y=(x-4)(x+5)\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00015">c. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00016">d. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00017">\(y=-5x(3-x)\)</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00018">e. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00019">f. _____</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            <para id="para-00020">What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph that represents \(y=x(x-2)\)?</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00022">\((0,0)\) and \((0, 2)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00023">\((0,0)\) and \((2, 0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00024">\((0,0)\) and \((0,-2)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00025">\((0,0)\) and \((-2,0)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00026">Correct! \((0,0)\) and \((2,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00028">The correct answer is: \((0,0)\) and \((2,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_66b54e19-d36a-4965-a9d9-1e3943173cdb" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00029">What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents \(y=x(x-2)\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00030">Correct! 1</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_37652284-a5ba-426c-839a-e975a25748c9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00033">What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph that represents \(y=(x-4)(x+5)\)?</para>
            <para id="para-00034">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00035">\((-5,0)\) and \((4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00036">\((0,-5)\) and \((0,4)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00037">\((5,0)\) and \((-4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00038">\((0,5)\) and \((0,-4)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00039">Correct! \((-5,0)\) and \((4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00040">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00041">The correct answer is: \((-5,0)\) and \((4,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4cac9766-6f18-4bcb-9ab9-7099ea97c8cf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            
            <para id="para-00042">What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents \(y=(x-4)(x+5)\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00043">Correct! -0.5</para>
            <para id="para-00044">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00045">The correct answer is -0.5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ee4f8051-bec4-4711-b7e4-0d39d4a1875d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00046">What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the graph that represents \(y=-5x(3-x)\)?</para>
            <para id="para-00047">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00048">\((0,0)\) and \((0,-3)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00049">\((0,0)\) and \((-3,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00050">\((0,0)\) and \((3,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00051">\((0,0)\) and \((0,3)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00052">Correct! \((0,0)\) and \((3,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00053">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is: \((0,0)\) and \((3,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f5018e25-e97d-48c6-b4e2-1557f6575971" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            
            <para id="para-00055">What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents \(y=-5x(3-x)\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00056">Correct! 1.5</para>
            <para id="para-00057">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00058">The correct answer is 1.5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ddcb53cd-215f-4142-a282-3ad0c570fa80" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            
            <para id="para-00059">What is the equation of the axis of symmetry of \(y = (x - 4)(x + 5)\)? (If needed, enter fractional values as a decimal.)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00060">Correct! -0.5</para>
            <para id="para-00061">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is -0.5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_693ff91a-6e94-4ba9-b34f-7bd5d58db355" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00063">Answer questions a–c about the function \(y=(x-2)(x-4)\).</para>
            <para id="para-00064">What are the \(x\)-intercepts of the vertex of the graph \(y=(x-2)(x-4)\).</para>
            <para id="para-00065">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00066">\((2,0)\) and \((4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00067">\((0,2)\) and \((0,4)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00068">\((-2,0)\) and \((-4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00069">\((0,-2)\) and \((0,-4)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00070">Correct! \((2,0)\) and \((4,0)\)</para>
            <para id="para-00071">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00072">The correct answer is: \((2,0)\) and \((4,0)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8376bb58-0f6a-4f6c-8301-ebf69e1887f9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00011">
            <para id="para-00073">Is \((-1,3)\) a point on the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00011">
            <para id="para-00074">Correct! Substituting -1 for \(x\) gives \((-1-2)(-1-4)\) or -3 -5, which is 15, so \((-1,15)\) would be a point on the graph, not \((-1,3)\).</para>
            <para id="para-00075">Try again. Revisit activities 7.11.2 and 7.11.3.</para>
            <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is No. Substituting -1 for \(x\) gives \((-1-2)(-1-4)\) or \(-3 \cdot  -5\), which is 15, so \((-1,15)\) would be a point on the graph, not \((-1,3)\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_70f17ceb-fe72-4533-98be-ce8ace7c8884" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            <para id="para-00077">Does the graph represent the equation \(y=(x-2)(x-4)\)? 
            
            (<media alt="Graph of nonlinear function, origin O. Horizontal axis from negative 8 to 6, by 2’s. Vertical axis from negative 8 to 12, by 4’s. Line passes through negative 7 comma 8, negative 5 comma 0, negative 3 comma 0 and 1 comma 7."><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_13_13_01.svg"/></media>)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            
            <para id="para-00078">Try again. Revisit activity 7.11.4.</para>
            <para id="para-00079">The correct answer is No.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content></document>